<title>BELGIUM: EU external trade surges on strong exports.</title>
<headline>EU external trade surges on strong exports.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Union trade with the rest of the world soared to 14.4 billion European currency units (Ecus) in the third quarter of last year, boosted by export growth of around 12.2 percent.</p>
<p>Figures released on Wednesday by the EU's statistical office Eurostat show that the 15-nation's bloc's trade surplus for the first nine month of last year amounted to 24.8 billion Ecus.</p>
<p>Germany and Italy recorded the biggest individual trade surpluses while Spain, Portugal and Austria had the smallest.</p>
